# signing

## This part of the project provides functions related to filling out and signing a VC

### Setup

To set up the project, follow these steps:

1. **Clone the repository:**

   ```sh
   git clone https://github.com/kaustabhbarman/vc-Supplychain.git
   cd <repository-directory>
   cd VC-SUPPLYCHAIN\signing\src

1. **Install dependencies:**

   ```sh
   npm install
This will install all the required dependencies listed in package.json.

## List of Functionalities:

## 1. Ethereum Account Creation Script

### Description

This script creates a new Ethereum account and saves the account details (address and private key) to a specified file. It uses the `web3` library to generate the account.

### Usage

To use the script, run the following command in your terminal:

    node createEthAccount.js <outputFilePath>

* <b>outputFilePath:</b> Path where the account details (address and private key) will be saved.
    
An example could be:

    node createEthAccount.js "../../VC Prototype/Battery Use Case/Lithium Miner/Identity Documents/ethereum-account.json"
    
## 2. DID Creation Script

### Description

This script creates a Decentralized Identifier (DID) and its associated DID Document. It uses the `ethr-did` library to generate the DID based on an Ethereum account. The script also allows you to specify an existing DID as the controller DID if needed. 

<b>In future iterations this DID Document will be stored on ethereum and adjusted to ethereums standards.</b>

### Usage

To use the script, run the following command in your terminal:

    node createDidDocument.js <outputFilePath> <accountDataFilePath> [<controllerDidFilePath>]

* <b>outputFilePath:</b> Path where the DID and DID Document will be saved.
* <b>accountDataFilePath:</b> Path to the file containing the Ethereum account details (address and private key).
* <b>controllerDidFilePath (Optional):</b> Path to the file containing an existing DID to use as the controller. If not provided, the newly created DID will be used as the controller.

an example could be:

    node createDidDocument.js "../../VC Prototype/Battery Use Case/Lithium Miner/Identity Documents/identity-did.json" "../../VC Prototype/Battery Use Case/Lithium Miner/Identity Documents/ethereum-account.json"

## 3. RSA Key Pair Generation Script

### Description

This script generates a new RSA key pair and saves both the private and public keys to a specified file. The script uses the `crypto` module to create the RSA key pair, and the keys are saved in PEM format.

### Usage

To use the script, run the following command in your terminal:

    node generateKeys.js <outputFilePath>

* <b>outputFilePath:</b> Path where the Key pair will be saved.

an example could be:

    node generateKeys.js "../../VC Prototype/Battery Use Case/Lithium Miner/Identity Documents/identity.txt"

## 4. JSON Signing Script

### Description

This script signs a JSON file using a JWS (JSON Web Signature) with the `RsaSignature2018` algorithm. It reads the JSON data, removes any existing proofs, generates a new signature using an RSA private key, and adds the proof to the JSON data. The updated JSON is then saved to the same file.

The script requires a private key in PEM format and a corresponding public key. Both keys should be stored in a file with specific headers and footers.

### Usage

To use the script, run the following command in your terminal:

    node signJson.js <inputFilePath> <identityPath> <role>

* <b>inputFilePath:</b> Path to the JSON file that you want to sign.
* <b>identityPath:</b> Path to the file containing the RSA private and public keys.
* <b>role:</b> The role of the entity signing the JSON. Valid roles are "issuer" or "holder".

an example could be:

    node signJson.js "../../VC Prototype/Battery Use Case/Lithium Miner/lithium-miner-vscc.json" "../../VC Prototype/Battery Use Case/Lithium Miner/Identity Documents/identity.txt" "issuer"
